# Let the gaius operator manage systemd units without sudo and without a polkit
# prompt, so `just restart` and the ACP restart executor run as the user,
# non-interactively, and never need `sudo -n`.
#
# Why: from a terminal `systemctl restart gaius.service` "works without sudo"
# only because polkit's agent asks for the user's OWN password; from a script or
# an agent the same call fails with "Interactive authentication required"
# (reset-failed probe, 2026-09-05). This host is Ubuntu 22.04 / polkit 0.105,
# which reads .pkla files under /etc/polkit-1/localauthority/ and does NOT read
# JavaScript .rules — and .pkla cannot match on the unit name, so this grants
# manage-units for all units to the operator. On this box that is no expansion:
# the operator already holds `(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` in sudoers. The scoping that
# matters — what an AGENT may restart — is not done here: the ACP agent never
# holds this permission; it writes a request and a root executor outside the
# unit performs the restart (docs/notes/2026-09-05/224300_acp_restart_rendezvous_protocol.md).
#
# Installed by `just reboot-hardening-install` into
# /etc/polkit-1/localauthority/50-local.d/. polkitd reloads .pkla on change.
[Allow the gaius operator to manage systemd units]
Identity=unix-user:rch
Action=org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units
ResultAny=yes
ResultInactive=yes
ResultActive=yes
